concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-10 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10 At the end of section 20"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-10 ;
    values:originalText "Add:  (9) The Commission must act fairly in the performance of the functions referred to in paragraph 11(1)(f).  (10) If a complaint is made under paragraph (1)(b), the Commission:  (a) must act expeditiously in dealing with the complaint; and  Schedule 2  Amendment of the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986  Human Rights Legislation Amendment Act 2017  Compilation date: 01/09/2021 Registered: 03/11/2021  (b) must use the Commission’s best endeavours to finish dealing with the complaint within 12 months after the complaint was made.  (11) Subsections (9) and (10) do not impose a duty on the Commission that is enforceable in court.  (12) Subsection (11) does not affect a legally enforceable obligation to observe the rules of natural justice." ;
    skos:definition "Add:  (9) The Commission must act fairly in the performance of the functions referred to in paragraph 11(1)(f).  (10) If a complaint is made under paragraph (1)(b), the Commission:  (a) must act expeditiously in dealing with the complaint; and  Schedule 2  Amendment of the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986  Human Rights Legislation Amendment Act 2017  Compilation date: 01/09/2021 Registered: 03/11/2021  (b) must use the Commission’s best endeavours to finish dealing with the complaint within 12 months after the complaint was made.  (11) Subsections (9) and (10) do not impose a duty on the Commission that is enforceable in court.  (12) Subsection (11) does not affect a legally enforceable obligation to observe the rules of natural justice."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f552a1e79bdc74d313b3f0f000e309faa363c9b81f8db6b9d0fb2b41f0dcea48" ;
    cof:pageNumber "7"^^xsd:integer ;
