concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-43 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "43 After subsection 46PH(1)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-43 ;
    values:originalText "Insert:  (1A) A complaint may be terminated under subsection (1) at any time, even if an inquiry into the complaint has begun.  Schedule 2  Amendment of the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986  Human Rights Legislation Amendment Act 2017  Compilation date: 01/09/2021 Registered: 03/11/2021  Mandatory termination of complaint  (1B) The President must terminate a complaint if the President is satisfied that:  (a) the complaint is trivial, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance; or  (b) there is no reasonable prospect of the matter being settled by conciliation.  (1C) The President must terminate a complaint if the President is satisfied that there would be no reasonable prospect that the Federal Court or the Federal Circuit Court would be satisfied that the alleged acts, omissions or practices are unlawful discrimination.  (1D) A complaint may be terminated under subsection (1B) or (1C) at any time, even if an inquiry into the complaint has begun." ;
    skos:definition "Insert:  (1A) A complaint may be terminated under subsection (1) at any time, even if an inquiry into the complaint has begun.  Schedule 2  Amendment of the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986  Human Rights Legislation Amendment Act 2017  Compilation date: 01/09/2021 Registered: 03/11/2021  Mandatory termination of complaint  (1B) The President must terminate a complaint if the President is satisfied that:  (a) the complaint is trivial, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance; or  (b) there is no reasonable prospect of the matter being settled by conciliation.  (1C) The President must terminate a complaint if the President is satisfied that there would be no reasonable prospect that the Federal Court or the Federal Circuit Court would be satisfied that the alleged acts, omissions or practices are unlawful discrimination.  (1D) A complaint may be terminated under subsection (1B) or (1C) at any time, even if an inquiry into the complaint has begun."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8445d5cfe714f4491bdd7be3a32948e53e2a96ef2d6d75ca8d501fbc73a359c4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "15"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-43-ss-1a ;
    cml:hasPart concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-43-ss-1b ;
    cml:hasPart concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-43-ss-1c ;
